msgid ""
"For an interobserver agreement study whose number of subjects is already "
"fixed, the lowest kappa the study would still be unable to rule out - the "
"lower bound of the one-sided confidence interval around the anticipated "
"kappa (kappa0); every value below it is excluded. Computed with the "
"kappaSize package. Use kappaSizePower to size a study for a hypothesis test "
"and kappaSizeCI to size it for a target interval width."
msgstr ""

#: R/cotest.b.R
msgid ""
"For orientation: most diagnostic tests fall between 0.60 and 0.95 for "
"sensitivity and between 0.70 and 0.98 for specificity, and prevalence is the "
"pre-test probability in the population you are testing (roughly 0.001-0.01 "
"for rare disease, 0.05-0.20 for common conditions). Values far outside these "
"bands are worth re-checking — most often sensitivity and specificity have "
"been entered the wrong way round."
